# Files that are read by Linux tools regardless of which platform edited them. A CRLF here is not a
# cosmetic difference: `backup.sh` checked out with CRLF fails as `/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r'`, and the
# same trailing byte breaks a Dockerfile `RUN` line and a Caddy directive.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
Dockerfile.dockerignore text eol=lf
Caddyfile text eol=lf
# Pasted into `crontab -e` on the Oracle VM, or copied there whole. cron reads a trailing \r as part
# of the command and the line then fails nightly, silently, in a log nobody is reading.
deploy/oracle/backup-cron.example text eol=lf

# The built avatar meshes (apps/normal-web/public/avatar3d). Committed on purpose — see
# docs/avatar-assets.md — and binary, so git never tries to normalise a line ending inside one
# or to show a diff of a hundred kilobytes of quantised vertices.
*.glb binary
